    in_dt
 {
+   /* Darwin on hakios: on the Adreno 730v3 what a draw reads of the framebuffer
+    * inside a batch came out wrong (blocks of a blurred backdrop, triangle by
+    * triangle, in CoreAnimation's vibrant layers); flushing after every draw
+    * mended it.  So a draw that reads the framebuffer starts a batch of its own:
+    * what is before it is in memory.  FD_FBFETCH_FLUSH=0 leaves it out.
